Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08.  FIXED (runtime macros).  The value of an assignment to a BOX place is the box: p-setf's fallback arm, `%store-back-form`'s box case (every compound assignment) and `p-.=`'s general arm answer the place box when it is one -- as p-scalar-= / p-my-= already did -- instead of box-set's own answer, which for a magic cell (the tied element's `:tielem` cell) is the setter's return, a copy.  So `setit($t{j} = "orig")`, `app($t{m} .= "n")`, `inc($t{n} += 2)`, `setit($t{o} ||= 5)` / `//=` / `*=`, a tied ARRAY element and a tied element through a ref are aliased; `($t{s} = "abc") =~ s/b/B/` (#4303's tied twin, it died "Modification of a read-only value") edits the element; FETCH / STORE counts = perl's on every row but `($t{v} += 1)++`.  Probes scratch/s536f/p/m3.pl m3b.pl m3c.pl m3d.pl.  Guard Pl/t/elem-assign-lvalue-01.t row 3 (FAILS on c8886b61).  Filed #4681: ++ / -- on an ASSIGNMENT re-evaluates it (`($x += f())++` calls f three times, untied too).  Not changed: an rvalue `my $y = ($h{a} = 5)` on a tied hash FETCHes nothing where perl FETCHes once (fidelity of counts only, the value is right).


